    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.28,
      338.7,
      549.75,
      364.0
    ],
    "text": "The rules published in Gazette Extraordinary No. 305 of July 6th 1984 as amended from time to time and last amended by Gazette Extraordinary No. 2117/17of April 3, 2019 are hereby further amended as follows :-",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT",
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.28,
      374.86,
      109.99,
      388.0
    ],
    "text": "1. In rule 19 -",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.28,
      398.86,
      492.41,
      412.0
    ],
    "text": "(a) by the repeal of paragraph (1) thereof and the substitution therefor, of the following paragraph : -",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      105.28,
      422.86,
      549.81,
      472.0
    ],
    "text": "\u201c (1) Where a member loses his membership in the Corporation under paragraph 1 of Rule 8, such member shall be paid a sum of Rupees Fifteen Thousand Rupees (Rs.15000/-) (hereinafter referred to as the Honorary Gratuity) for each and every month for a period of six months from the date of retirement totally amounting to ninety thousand rupees (Rs.90,000/-)\u201d;",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.28,
      482.86,
      520.47,
      496.0
    ],
    "text": "(b) by the repeal of sub paragraph (4) thereof and the substitution therefor, of the following sub paragraph -",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      105.28,
      506.86,
      549.8,
      568.0
    ],
    "text": "\u201c(4) Every member who wishes to become entitled for the Honorary Gratuity shall make a contribution of Rupees Four Thousand Five Hundred (Rs.4500/-) per annum at the rate of Rupees Three Hundred and Seventy five (Rs 375/-) per month for a period of ten years. All recoveries in respect of honorary gratuity shall be deposited in a fixed deposit in a State Bank. The interest accrued from the fixed deposit shall be credited to the honorary gratuity savings account and shall be used for the payment of honorary gratuity;\u201d",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.29,
      578.86,
      110.0,
      592.0
    ],
    "text": "2. In rule 21 -",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      55.29,
      602.86,
      472.42,
      616.0
    ],
    "text": "(a) by the repeal of paragraph (1) thereof and substitution therefor, of the following paragraph -",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      105.29,
      626.86,
      549.81,
      688.0
    ],
    "text": "\u201c Festival Loans (l) (a) Any member who has completed a period of one year as a member and wishes to obtain festival loan shall be entitled to such loan of Rupees Twenty-Five Thousand (Rs. 25000/-) once a year. Any member who has obtained the said festival loan shall settle such amount together with an interest at the rate of twelve per centum (12%) in ten monthly installments of Rupees Two Thousand and five Hundred (Rs 2500/-).",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      105.3,
      698.86,
      549.81,
      724.0
    ],
    "text": "(b) No member shall be entitled to obtain a festival loan, until any previous festival loan obtained by him if any , is fully settled by such member .",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRomanPSMT"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
